\title{WHIR}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    The current endpoint of the lineage: a multilinear commitment with a very fast verifier, unifying the Reed–Solomon proximity line with the tensor-commitment line that Basefold began.
}

\p{
    To work through:
    \ul{
        \li{The construction, and where [sumcheck](dhsorens-002Q) enters the low-degree test.}
        \li{How a multilinear claim is served by a univariate proximity test — the translation, and its cost.}
        \li{The verifier-time claim, and what it is measured against.}
        \li{Which of [STIR](dhsorens-003B)'s ideas it keeps and which it discards.}
        \li{ArkLib's WHIR formalisation: what is proved, and what the remaining obligations are.}
    }
}

\p{
    Sources: Arnon, Chiesa, Fenzi, and Yogev, \em{WHIR}; [SoK: Hash-Based Polynomial Commitments](https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/1367); [ArkLib](https://github.com/Verified-zkEVM/ArkLib).
}
